(4655465, 671785, 92844, '<td valign="top">Good depth of field, and a good subject, however... 1)no bugs unless the bugs are the focus of the photograph 2)Composition? Lots of empty space. Try a square or make the subjects slightly larger in the frame 3)No border. Would you hang a photo on the wall with a border like that? If a border is a must, go with white. 4) Color has blown out the detail in the pedals. Rich detail is what makes an engaging photo. Don''t saturate it quite so much and carfully manage the levels curve. 5)Color balance it away from yellow a little... magenta could use a slight boost as could blue. Please don''t take these the wrong way... I love the cluster of flowers (and actually this would make a beautiful fine art monochrome photo) but just try the suggestions and see what happens!</td>', 'Good depth of field, and a good subject, however... 1)no bugs unless the bugs are the focus of the photograph 2)Composition? Lots of empty space. Try a square or make the subjects slightly larger in the frame 3)No border. Would you hang a photo on the wall with a border like that? If a border is a must, go with white. 4) Color has blown out the detail in the pedals. Rich detail is what makes an engaging photo. Don''t saturate it quite so much and carfully manage the levels curve. 5)Color balance it away from yellow a little... magenta could use a slight boost as could blue. Please don''t take these the wrong way... I love the cluster of flowers (and actually this would make a beautiful fine art monochrome photo) but just try the suggestions and see what happens!', '2008-04-23 13:08:08.000000', NULL, 1),
